All issues have been resolved and the requested features have been implemented:

Key Updates & Fixes Implemented
1. 3D Bomb Visibility Debugged & Fixed
Instant Initialization: The 3D bomb is now built immediately on scene startup (build3DBomb() in init3DScene()). You no longer have to click through dialogue to have the bomb render.
Full-Screen 100% Viewport: The default layout is now pure full-screen 3D bomb. The bomb sits front-and-center, framed by camera preset (0, 16, 17) looking at (0, 0, 0).
Automatic Viewport Sizing: Added window resize handlers to the briefing close, manual drawer toggle, and level transitions so the canvas always renders at full screen resolution.
2. Strict Level Locking (Level 2 Cannot Be Accessed Early)
Locked levels are strictly enforced via highestUnlockedLevel = 1.
The HUD displays LVL 1, 🔒 LVL 2, 🔒 LVL 3, 🔒 LVL 4, 🔒 LVL 5.
Locked pills are dimmed with cursor: not-allowed. Clicking a locked level triggers a warning buzzer and alerts:
"LEVEL X IS LOCKED! You must successfully defuse Level X-1 before attempting Level X."
Level 2 only unlocks when Level 1 is defused and the "SUCCESSFUL!" debrief screen is reached.
3. Field Manual Only Shows When Selected
The manual is completely hidden by default, leaving your screen unobstructed.
Clicking the 📖 FIELD MANUAL button in the top bar smoothly slides out a tactical manual drawer from the right.
Click ✕ CLOSE [ESC] or press the ESC / M key to slide it back away.
4. English Spoken Voice & Simplified Dialogue
English Voice: Integrated native Web Speech API (SpeechSynthesis with en-US voice) so Sgt. Vance speaks to you aloud in clear, authoritative military English.
Removed Alien Chirps: Removed the rapid synthesizer chirp sound loops that sounded like gibberish / foreign speech.
Immediate Defuse Option: Added an instant ⏩ DEFUSE BOMB NOW [SKIP] button on every dialogue card so you can jump straight to disarming without waiting.
5. Level-Filtered Manual (Only Shows Active Level)
When on Level 1, the manual displays only:
The Master Color Code Matrix (0-9 reference)
The Level 1 Recruit instructions & schematics
Tabs and sections for Levels 2, 3, 4, 5 are completely hidden!
When you progress to Level 2, the manual automatically updates to show only Level 2.
6. Rich Visual Pictures & Schematics in the Manual
3-Wire Circuit Schematic (FIG 1.1): Visual diagram showing Wire 1 (Red), Wire 2 (Yellow) with scissors badge & green glowing cut indicator (★ CUT WIRE #2 (YELLOW) ★), and Wire 3 (Blue).
Keypad Decoder Diagram (FIG 1.2): Illustrated flow showing Red (2) → Yellow (4) → Green (5) translating directly into PIN: 245.
4-Band Resistor Schematic: Resistor diagram showing Yellow, Violet, Orange, and Gold bands totaling 47 kΩ.
Logic Gate Circuit Schematic: Electronic diagram of Switch A, B, and C with AND & XOR gates.
Sgt. Vance Field Portrait & Tactical Seals.
7. Clean Top Bar (Removed Clutter)
Removed Split Co-Op, Pop-out Manual, SFX toggle, and CRT scanlines.
Removed the song volume slider; the Suno soundtrack now plays at a comfortable, balanced background volume (0.35).
8. High-Tech Tactical Bunker 3D Background
Tactical Workbench Surface: Procedural brushed-metal workbench with cybernetic cyan grid markings, targeting reticles directly beneath the bomb chassis, hazard caution borders, and sector coordinates.
Industrial Bunker Wall & Support Girders: Heavy concrete and steel structure behind the workspace.
Telemetry Server Racks: Dual electronic server racks flanking the background with independently blinking green, cyan, and amber status LEDs.
Overhead Fluorescent Fixture: Heavy-duty hanging industrial lamp casting warm lighting and soft shadows onto the ordnance.
Atmospheric Floating Dust Particles: Subtle particle field drifting through the spotlight beam.
